    "statement": "The fragment “these and many other sociopolitical issues” (line 7) is a compound object of the verb “address.” 1 4 7 10 11 In the early days of political action on climate change adaptation was seen as, at best, a poor relation to cutting greenhouse-gas emissions—at worst as a distraction. In his first book on the subject, “Earth in the Balance” (1992), Al Gore, who became America’s vice -president the following year, described it as “a kind of laziness.” In 2010, with attempts to agree on reductions in emissions stalled by the failure of the Copenhagen summit, and with emissions rising steeply as the world bounced back from the financial crisis of 2007 -09, adaptation began to take its proper place as a topic of international concern. Climate adaptation policies are needed more than ever. The Economist. May 30th, 2020. https://www.economist.com/schools- brief/2020/05/30/climate-adaptation-policies-are-needed-more-than-ever. Concerning syntactic and morphological aspects, judge the following items.",
