    "topicId": "",
    "statement": "The word “began” is in the simple past tense. 1 4 7 10 12 George Orwell’s fiction has been prescient, invoked to describe the ills of nearly every age. 1984 has repeatedly topped English -language bestseller lists, including in 1954 (the year the BBC did a television adaptation), 1984 and 2003 (the centenary of Orwell’s birth). Political events bring Orwell new readers, including Donald Trump’s inauguration in 2017 and fomenting of the riot at America’s Capitol in 2021. After Russia’s invasion of Ukraine last year, 1984 became the most -downloaded electronic fiction book in Russia. It is thus no surprise that in 2023, with fears of autocracy and intense culture wars, the man who wrote so skilfully about dark subjects is back in the spotlight. Interest in George Orwell and his dystopian fiction is high. The Economist. August 4th 2023. https://www.economist.com/culture/2023/08/04/interest-in-george-orwell- and-his-dystopian-fiction-is-high Based on the text and considering phonological aspects of the English language, judge the following items.",
